00:47:19.145 --> 00:47:23.880
You created what you might
call a director's commentary

00:47:23.880 --> 00:47:28.110
that you would then see in the documentary

00:47:28.110 --> 00:47:30.600
about your DJ debut, but you folded it

00:47:30.600 --> 00:47:33.480
into the actual debut
itself, if that makes sense.

00:47:33.480 --> 00:47:35.255
This is the director's commentary.

00:47:35.255 --> 00:47:37.384
You see me up there on stage.
Yeah, yeah.

00:47:37.384 --> 00:47:39.780
I was questioning my entire life,

00:47:39.780 --> 00:47:40.613
but no, you're just like,

00:47:40.613 --> 00:47:42.090
I'm questioning my entire life right now.

00:47:42.090 --> 00:47:43.311
I don't know how many people

00:47:43.311 --> 00:47:46.740
and people, I think most
people experienced it as,

00:47:46.740 --> 00:47:49.410
Link is very weird and very odd.

00:47:49.410 --> 00:47:50.310
And I'm not surprised,

00:47:50.310 --> 00:47:51.600
'cause I know him.
And that's everything

00:47:51.600 --> 00:47:54.150
that I expected, and so
that kind of makes this fun

00:47:54.150 --> 00:47:56.070
and cool and enjoyable, which it did,

00:47:56.070 --> 00:47:58.590
but I think probably
some people were like,

00:47:58.590 --> 00:48:01.860
oh he's, it is performance art,

00:48:01.860 --> 00:48:04.320
but it's honest performance art.

00:48:04.320 --> 00:48:06.813
I, when I went up there on that stage,

00:48:09.510 --> 00:48:11.640
I was not nervous.

00:48:11.640 --> 00:48:14.542
I went from three weeks earlier
to being a complete wreck

00:48:14.542 --> 00:48:19.542
to determining that with my
criteria and like, you know,

00:48:20.580 --> 00:48:22.221
that like I wasn't gonna lose perspective

00:48:22.221 --> 00:48:26.400
and I was not gonna
let go of my insistence

00:48:26.400 --> 00:48:29.040
on having the time of my life,

00:48:29.040 --> 00:48:34.040
and I am so, I've never
had anything that I felt

00:48:34.511 --> 00:48:39.060
so much pressure and
then got past it so that

00:48:39.060 --> 00:48:44.060
when it happened I could
just be just there for it,

00:48:45.360 --> 00:48:50.130
and let me tell you, I
actually, that was my experience

00:48:50.130 --> 00:48:53.730
and we've done a lot of stuff
that I wish I could go back

00:48:53.730 --> 00:48:55.867
and be able to pull that mind trick

00:48:55.867 --> 00:49:00.867
and, but something about
the setting was so special

00:49:00.900 --> 00:49:03.870
that the safety net was so supportive.

00:49:03.870 --> 00:49:04.703
Yeah.

00:49:04.703 --> 00:49:08.550
That it's not, you know,
it's unrealistic to expect

00:49:08.550 --> 00:49:13.550
that I could go back and
apply it 100% to something

00:49:14.040 --> 00:49:15.810
in the past or even in
the future for like,

00:49:15.810 --> 00:49:19.740
our next demanding thing
that like, 'cause you know,

00:49:19.740 --> 00:49:22.800
there was also like, nothing
really depends on this.

00:49:22.800 --> 00:49:25.440
You know, it's like if
I fall flat on my face,

00:49:25.440 --> 00:49:27.930
I'm just gonna get up and
keep going and make a joke,

00:49:27.930 --> 00:49:30.019
because once we got
past all of this stuff,

00:49:30.019 --> 00:49:35.019
like this opening part, I still
didn't speak the entire set.

00:49:35.640 --> 00:49:40.640
I just started playing my set
and I had a decent number,

00:49:41.790 --> 00:49:45.274
I had a bunch of ideas for how
I wanted to transition stuff,

00:49:45.274 --> 00:49:50.274
and I would say a third of the time,

00:49:50.522 --> 00:49:55.522
I pretty much accomplished
what I was going for

00:49:56.280 --> 00:49:57.540
a third of the time.

00:49:57.540 --> 00:49:58.740
Okay.

00:49:58.740 --> 00:50:02.940
And I think that a lot
of things like, you know,

00:50:02.940 --> 00:50:05.560
a lot of times it, I would
just, I'd hit the button

00:50:06.608 --> 00:50:08.010
and I would say like, Elkhound .

00:50:08.010 --> 00:50:09.423
Yeah.

00:50:09.423 --> 00:50:11.815
Well, over half the time
that I played Elkhound,

00:50:11.815 --> 00:50:16.320
I was trying to cue the
next song in my headphones.

00:50:16.320 --> 00:50:17.153
Okay.

00:50:17.153 --> 00:50:19.260
It did often come at interesting times.

00:50:19.260 --> 00:50:20.550
Yeah, it was never.

00:50:20.550 --> 00:50:21.600
He's making some interesting choices.

00:50:21.600 --> 00:50:23.820
I was like, 'cause I'll
listen on my headphones

00:50:23.820 --> 00:50:25.590
and I'm queuing up the song
and you can't hear that,

00:50:25.590 --> 00:50:26.700
but somehow the Elkhound.
Yeah.

00:50:26.700 --> 00:50:28.800
You can't predict.
Still goes out there.

00:50:28.800 --> 00:50:30.629
What Elkhound or Snugglebaby.

00:50:30.629 --> 00:50:32.376
I'll be, oh I just said
Elkhound by accident.

00:50:32.376 --> 00:50:33.209
I better say Snugglebaby now,

00:50:33.209 --> 00:50:34.407
and then I would hit
Snugglebaby and then I would

00:50:34.407 --> 00:50:36.155
cue my thing and it just got.

00:50:36.155 --> 00:50:36.988
And it got a cheer every time.

00:50:36.988 --> 00:50:38.760
It got a cheer every time,
and it got to a point

00:50:38.760 --> 00:50:41.190
where I was like, oh, I'm
screwing up, and if you just act

00:50:41.190 --> 00:50:44.450
like I meant to do it, after
that intro that I gave,

00:50:44.450 --> 00:50:47.250
they're gonna believe that
I'm meant to do everything.

00:50:47.250 --> 00:50:49.200
Like, even when I played the speech,

00:50:49.200 --> 00:50:51.985
like after like 45
seconds into the speech,

00:50:51.985 --> 00:50:55.248
I accidentally started the speech over.

00:50:55.248 --> 00:50:56.081
Yeah, I thought that was intentional.

00:50:56.081 --> 00:50:58.770
And I was like, oh that's,
yeah, that's a weird choice.

00:50:58.770 --> 00:51:00.132
I'm going on instinct now.

00:51:01.134 --> 00:51:03.510
I guess my body wanted that to
be even weirder than it was.

00:51:03.510 --> 00:51:05.910
So I gave the speech twice, the first half

00:51:05.910 --> 00:51:10.020
of the speech twice,
and then it was weird.

00:51:10.020 --> 00:51:13.062
Maybe I just got looser,
I got some confidence,

00:51:13.062 --> 00:51:17.430
but there were a couple
of points towards the end

00:51:17.430 --> 00:51:21.126
of the set, like I was gonna
go from Michael McDonald,

00:51:21.126 --> 00:51:26.126
"I Keep Forgetting," into
"Regulate" by, you know,

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:32.899
the G-Funk Classic, which samples it,

00:51:32.899 --> 00:51:37.899
and I could not get "Regulate" to play.

00:51:38.160 --> 00:51:40.710
I could not, I don't, I still don't know.

00:51:40.710 --> 00:51:41.700
You don't know what happened?

00:51:41.700 --> 00:51:43.481
I couldn't transition to the next song,

00:51:43.481 --> 00:51:46.200
and that's why like, I keep forgetting

00:51:46.200 --> 00:51:47.962
it went away to nothing.

00:51:47.962 --> 00:51:49.347
People would always cheer 'cause they,

00:51:49.347 --> 00:51:51.450
it was like, oh he's
going to the next song.

00:51:51.450 --> 00:51:54.540
They're so gracious, and
then I'm like struggling

00:51:54.540 --> 00:51:56.194
to figure out why the song's not playing,

00:51:56.194 --> 00:51:58.860
and then I ended up having
to go back and just play more

00:51:58.860 --> 00:52:00.480
of Michael McDonald 'cause
I couldn't figure out

00:52:00.480 --> 00:52:03.390
how to get to it and I was
like, well, okay, I just move on

00:52:03.390 --> 00:52:05.700
and then, and that was in
the latter half of the set,

00:52:05.700 --> 00:52:09.540
and then the next like, so by
the time we got to the ending,

00:52:09.540 --> 00:52:13.650
like I had, the other thing
was things got squirrelly

00:52:13.650 --> 00:52:18.060
'cause I had so much music,
but I had like an hour of music

00:52:18.060 --> 00:52:20.280
I wanted to play and I
had 15 minutes to play it.

00:52:20.280 --> 00:52:22.990
So I had to start making
choices of what I was skipping

00:52:22.990 --> 00:52:23.823
and what I was playing.
Because there's

00:52:23.823 --> 00:52:26.310
a noise ordinance that we had to abide by.

00:52:26.310 --> 00:52:28.470
Well yeah, at a certain point
you just gotta wrap it up.

00:52:28.470 --> 00:52:31.560
It was, I mean, it was after
midnight and so I'm making

00:52:31.560 --> 00:52:34.200
all these choices on the fly
and then trying to figure out

00:52:34.200 --> 00:52:36.570
how I'm gonna transition from song to song

00:52:36.570 --> 00:52:39.210
between songs I've never,
it's never, I've never.

00:52:39.210 --> 00:52:42.703
I'm literally doing
everything in the moment

00:52:42.703 --> 00:52:47.703
and that's what got the
best of me that when I like,

00:52:47.790 --> 00:52:49.635
these fundamental mistakes, like,

00:52:49.635 --> 00:52:51.420
oh, this slider's over here.

00:52:51.420 --> 00:52:53.942
So this song is never, they're
never gonna hear this song.

00:52:53.942 --> 00:52:57.060
So the set kind of just
started to fall apart

00:52:57.060 --> 00:53:01.709
a little bit by the end but,
and then at the very end

00:53:01.709 --> 00:53:05.010
I did get the microphone and I
gave a speech and I was like,

00:53:05.010 --> 00:53:07.643
you know what, all good
things must come to an end.

00:53:07.643 --> 00:53:08.476
Thanks for coming out to Mythicon.

00:53:08.476 --> 00:53:11.580
This has been amazing and then I pressed,

00:53:11.580 --> 00:53:13.720
I had it all cued up and I was pressing,

00:53:13.720 --> 00:53:16.860
I was gonna play the
last song, "Roll Out."

00:53:16.860 --> 00:53:18.137
Yep.

00:53:18.137 --> 00:53:19.159
So that everybody could leave.

00:53:19.159 --> 00:53:20.163
Yep.

00:53:20.163 --> 00:53:21.167
By Ludacris,

00:53:21.167 --> 00:53:22.189
wouldn't play.

00:53:22.189 --> 00:53:23.022
Yeah, yeah.

00:53:23.022 --> 00:53:23.855
It would not play.

00:53:23.855 --> 00:53:24.688
Was that when you started saying, I don't,

00:53:24.688 --> 00:53:25.694
I can't get the last song to play?

00:53:25.694 --> 00:53:26.527
Yeah, that's when I
said, I would end this.

00:53:26.527 --> 00:53:27.913
I thought that might be part of.

00:53:27.913 --> 00:53:28.746
If I could get the last song to play.

00:53:28.746 --> 00:53:30.325
The beautiful thing about your style.

00:53:30.325 --> 00:53:31.837
And everybody left.

00:53:31.837 --> 00:53:32.841
Is that anything could be intentional.

00:53:32.841 --> 00:53:33.867
Anything.

00:53:33.867 --> 00:53:34.867
Or unintentionally, no one knows.

00:53:34.867 --> 00:53:36.240
Yes, except for now.

00:53:36.240 --> 00:53:37.080
Yeah, now they know.

00:53:37.080 --> 00:53:40.074
So now when people come to my
sets, they're gonna be like,

00:53:40.074 --> 00:53:42.420
oh, it must all be a mistake.

00:53:42.420 --> 00:53:43.253
Yeah, right.

00:53:43.253 --> 00:53:44.100
But nope, I'm gonna get better.

00:53:44.100 --> 00:53:46.020
It's all gonna be intentional,
and then I finally

00:53:46.020 --> 00:53:49.943
got "Roll Out" to play and
then when "Roll Out" was over,

00:53:49.943 --> 00:53:54.943
I had one more song queued
up, like my walk off song

00:53:55.207 --> 00:53:58.800
and I pressed it, nothing happened,

00:53:58.800 --> 00:54:00.180
and I just walked off stage.

00:54:00.180 --> 00:54:01.013
Yeah.

00:54:01.013 --> 00:54:04.500
And it was just like, I was
like, this has been amazing.

00:54:04.500 --> 00:54:07.890
I'm not gonna let any of this
get to me, and I was ecstatic,

00:54:07.890 --> 00:54:10.748
but there was some, in my mind
there was some huge fails,

00:54:10.748 --> 00:54:15.450
but the biggest thing about it
was, I was up there on stage

00:54:15.450 --> 00:54:17.910
and I was like in, I was
in this world of like,

00:54:17.910 --> 00:54:19.664
okay, I'm gonna get started.

00:54:19.664 --> 00:54:21.969
I didn't have my headphones.

00:54:21.969 --> 00:54:23.940
So like right at the beginning I'm like.

00:54:23.940 --> 00:54:26.401
Yeah, there's a lot of details.

00:54:26.401 --> 00:54:30.690
I lean over to, and like Jenna walks up,

00:54:30.690 --> 00:54:32.760
and right, you walked
up and Ben walked up.

00:54:32.760 --> 00:54:33.852
I, well I could see.

00:54:33.852 --> 00:54:35.576
I was like.

00:54:35.576 --> 00:54:36.975
I was lost.
I could tell

00:54:36.975 --> 00:54:37.860
by your body language
that something was wrong.

00:54:37.860 --> 00:54:39.227
Right.

00:54:39.227 --> 00:54:40.376
I was like, I was looking around.

00:54:40.376 --> 00:54:41.209
A DJ without his headphones.

00:54:41.209 --> 00:54:45.240
I was looking at the other
DJ's headphones and their,

00:54:45.240 --> 00:54:48.900
his jacks were too big
'cause he's a big time DJ.

00:54:48.900 --> 00:54:50.453
He's got an eighth inch jack.
I didn't wanna say

00:54:50.453 --> 00:54:51.960
how big his deck was, but his deck was.

00:54:51.960 --> 00:54:53.850
His deck was twice as big as mine.

00:54:53.850 --> 00:54:54.683
Maybe four times.

00:54:54.683 --> 00:54:58.200
Okay, yeah, and his jacks
were twice as big in my jack.

00:54:58.200 --> 00:55:00.870
So I leaned over to Jenna, I
was like, I need my headphones.

00:55:00.870 --> 00:55:05.220
They're in my computer bag in
the other house in the top,

00:55:05.220 --> 00:55:08.026
and then come to find out,
Jenna sprints over there and I.

00:55:08.026 --> 00:55:08.859
Sprinted.

00:55:08.859 --> 00:55:11.220
I started the speech, so
I'm doing the speech now,

00:55:11.220 --> 00:55:12.588
and then Jenna, when you came back,

00:55:12.588 --> 00:55:14.370
you fell flat on your face.

00:55:14.370 --> 00:55:15.510
Oh, I ate it.

00:55:15.510 --> 00:55:16.890
Oh, bad, yeah.

00:55:16.890 --> 00:55:19.680
I sprinted all the way to the house.

00:55:19.680 --> 00:55:21.570
I like, there was some
crew members in there

00:55:21.570 --> 00:55:23.341
and I was like, emergency, out of the way,

00:55:23.341 --> 00:55:25.500
and I like grabbed your headphones,

00:55:25.500 --> 00:55:29.100
sprinted all the way back,
and then bound up the stairs

00:55:29.100 --> 00:55:32.400
and I hit the last stair
to the stage and just, bam.

00:55:32.400 --> 00:55:33.516
In front of everybody.

00:55:33.516 --> 00:55:34.349
In front of everybody, ate it.

00:55:34.349 --> 00:55:36.467
Straight down on my knees.
I did not see this.

00:55:36.467 --> 00:55:37.997
Elkhound was in his own world,

00:55:37.997 --> 00:55:41.385
'cause I was giving my speech.

00:55:41.385 --> 00:55:42.406
About half the audience.

00:55:42.406 --> 00:55:43.413
I was giving my speech.

00:55:43.413 --> 00:55:44.992
Jenna was falling on her face.

00:55:44.992 --> 00:55:46.230
Your headphones were like, silver.

00:55:46.230 --> 00:55:49.230
They were just Christy's
headphones from going on planes.

00:55:49.230 --> 00:55:50.137
But how big were they?

00:55:50.137 --> 00:55:52.860
They were like Bose headphones.

00:55:52.860 --> 00:55:54.077
They weren't too big.
Okay.

00:55:54.077 --> 00:55:54.910
Yeah, for some reason I can't picture 'em.

00:55:54.910 --> 00:55:59.043
But then I'm looking around
and the crew is on stage.

00:56:01.290 --> 00:56:04.410
Lily's on stage, Lincoln's on stage.

00:56:04.410 --> 00:56:07.860
My dad is on stage, they're all dancing.

00:56:07.860 --> 00:56:09.518
Christy's on stage.

00:56:09.518 --> 00:56:10.522
Yeah, she was.

00:56:10.522 --> 00:56:11.880
You know, Christy's not in the public eye.

00:56:11.880 --> 00:56:14.580
She made a choice that
she was gonna be out there

00:56:14.580 --> 00:56:19.580
supporting me and it was
just a, it was so sweet.

00:56:19.804 --> 00:56:21.240
It was beautiful.

00:56:21.240 --> 00:56:22.380
You were on stage.

00:56:22.380 --> 00:56:23.213
I was.

00:56:23.213 --> 00:56:26.670
David Hill was like my hype
man over on the other side.

00:56:26.670 --> 00:56:27.570
David Hill has a gift.

00:56:27.570 --> 00:56:28.889
Oh my God.

00:56:28.889 --> 00:56:29.722
I can't go anywhere without that guy now.

00:56:29.722 --> 00:56:34.722
He is amazing, and like
when I played "New Light,"

00:56:34.800 --> 00:56:37.140
which is like me and
Lily and Lincoln's song,

00:56:37.140 --> 00:56:38.520
like they came over and I put my arms

00:56:38.520 --> 00:56:39.750
around 'em and we're dancing.

00:56:39.750 --> 00:56:41.310
That's also not something
you typically see

00:56:41.310 --> 00:56:43.770
at a DJ set, is it?

00:56:43.770 --> 00:56:45.123
The DJ's kids.
They're like.

00:56:45.123 --> 00:56:45.963
Yeah.

00:56:45.963 --> 00:56:47.370
Come up and dance with him,

00:56:47.370 --> 00:56:49.230
but again, I was thinking
that at the time.

00:56:49.230 --> 00:56:51.960
I was like, what a interesting,

00:56:51.960 --> 00:56:54.576
I was just, I'd been thinking about this.

00:56:54.576 --> 00:56:56.178
Tell me what you thought about

00:56:56.178 --> 00:56:57.368
the whole thing that you had said.

00:56:57.368 --> 00:56:59.730
Well, I was thinking the way that it was

00:56:59.730 --> 00:57:03.699
a great culmination to Mythicon in general

00:57:03.699 --> 00:57:08.699
because I was like, what
an interesting world that,

00:57:08.760 --> 00:57:11.430
you know, the two of us and our team

00:57:11.430 --> 00:57:14.851
and the Mythical Beasts
have created in which this,

00:57:14.851 --> 00:57:17.640
what is happening right now is possible.

00:57:17.640 --> 00:57:21.630
Like you, your dad from Myrtle,

00:57:21.630 --> 00:57:25.056
north Myrtle Beach, South
Carolina is up there like.

00:57:25.056 --> 00:57:26.590
Dancing to JID.

00:57:26.590 --> 00:57:28.050
Doing his dance.

00:57:28.050 --> 00:57:29.601
Dancing a jig to JID.

00:57:29.601 --> 00:57:34.601
And you know, on the same
stage where the night before,

00:57:36.532 --> 00:57:39.840
Jessie and I had done
this country music thing.

00:57:39.840 --> 00:57:40.673
Wild, man.

00:57:40.673 --> 00:57:43.140
For the same, essentially
the same group of people,

00:57:43.140 --> 00:57:44.820
and then your kids are up there.

00:57:44.820 --> 00:57:45.960
My, Shepard's up there like.

00:57:45.960 --> 00:57:46.793
Shepard's up there.

00:57:46.793 --> 00:57:49.099
Shepard's trying to get
a dance a little bit.

00:57:49.099 --> 00:57:50.140
Yeah, it was awesome.

00:57:50.140 --> 00:57:51.979
And I was just like this, yeah.

00:57:51.979 --> 00:57:56.220
I was, so in terms of
that, I was just like,

00:57:56.220 --> 00:57:59.190
what a inter, what an
incredible atmosphere

00:57:59.190 --> 00:58:00.843
for this kind of thing to happen,

00:58:02.155 --> 00:58:07.155
and then, I mean, ultimately
I was thinking this is,

00:58:10.020 --> 00:58:12.270
I don't think anything that
you did was surprising.

00:58:12.270 --> 00:58:14.970
I think that all of it was, I didn't know.

00:58:14.970 --> 00:58:16.470
None of it

00:58:16.470 --> 00:58:17.768
was expected.
I've learned that.

00:58:17.768 --> 00:58:19.340
You couldn't have expected anything I did.

00:58:19.340 --> 00:58:23.880
If you had asked me what
mistakes did you make

00:58:23.880 --> 00:58:25.813
that I picked up on, I would be like,

00:58:25.813 --> 00:58:29.381
well, obviously the end when
he couldn't play that song,

