But one of the things that
I was able to observe,

01:09:19.800 --> 01:09:21.720
even in a really supportive crowd like

01:09:21.720 --> 01:09:23.970
all the Mythical Beasts, is that if,

01:09:23.970 --> 01:09:26.490
you could put two songs, you know,

01:09:26.490 --> 01:09:30.412
you could show me two
songs and BPM is the same,

01:09:30.412 --> 01:09:34.050
perceived, like energy is the same.

01:09:34.050 --> 01:09:34.883
Yes.

01:09:34.883 --> 01:09:36.090
And I would be like, yeah, both of these

01:09:36.090 --> 01:09:40.890
are like, crowd hype inducing
songs, and then it turns out

01:09:40.890 --> 01:09:44.190
that for whatever intangible
reason that is very difficult

01:09:44.190 --> 01:09:47.100
to anticipate, no, only
one of them is what

01:09:47.100 --> 01:09:48.420
the crowd is gonna like.

01:09:48.420 --> 01:09:49.253
Right.

01:09:49.253 --> 01:09:51.300
And that to me is what something clicked.

01:09:51.300 --> 01:09:52.590
That's when something
clicked for me is like,

01:09:52.590 --> 01:09:55.140
oh, that's really the job of a DJ.

01:09:55.140 --> 01:09:56.820
They can't, you know, people.

01:09:56.820 --> 01:09:58.334
And knowing what's gonna happen.

01:09:58.334 --> 01:09:59.370
Yeah, and they're not gonna,

01:09:59.370 --> 01:10:01.440
it's, they don't wanna fake it, you know?

01:10:01.440 --> 01:10:02.790
Even my friends didn't wanna fake it

01:10:02.790 --> 01:10:03.960
and they were just like, come on and play,

01:10:03.960 --> 01:10:06.360
and I finally got 'em
with that, and then I,

01:10:06.360 --> 01:10:07.860
so I played a couple of
songs and I was like,

01:10:07.860 --> 01:10:09.810
